 "description": "T26 MySQL SERVER + spatial reference system low-frequency DDL (issue #105), R3 stage manifest — scope is recognition, named boundaries, and output redaction ONLY. The four baseline anchors and their db_* required cases are declared so a future separately-authorized native run executes unchanged; no SERVER/SRS lifecycle semantics are claimed. cli_cases pin: four SERVER forms (create/alter/drop/drop-if-exists) as named unaudited boundaries on mysql and vendor boundaries on tidb; six SRS forms (create, create+IF NOT EXISTS, create OR REPLACE, drop, drop+IF EXISTS, plus bare create) as implementation boundaries on mysql and vendor on tidb; strict whole-input rejects (trailing junk, missing FDW clause, negative/overflow SRID, OR REPLACE + IF NOT EXISTS contradiction) as parser errors; ALTER INSTANCE inventory subactions RELOAD TLS (with NO ROLLBACK ON ERROR member recorded) and ROTATE INNODB MASTER KEY as precise named boundaries; and fixed-shape output redaction proving no credential/definition payload reaches raw_sql, normalized_sql, unsupported[].sql, or markdown.",
